It should pretty print pure JS inside a script tag
printWidth: 20
<script>
function main(){console.log("hello");}const x = 100 > 42 ? x : y;
</script>

It should pretty print json inside a script tag
<script type="application/json">
{
"a":[1,2,3],
"b": "string"
}
</script>

It should pretty print typescript
<script type="application/x-typescript">
type Node = TwigNode|HtmlNode|TextNode
type TwigNode = TwigDrop|TwigTag
function print(node:Node){return node.toString();}
</script>

It should pretty print markdown (?) why not!?
<div>
<script type="text/markdown">
# heading
* item
* item
  * item
* item
</script>
</div>

It should fallback to reindenting when it can't parse the source
(e.g. because of Twig in JS)
printWidth: 20
<script>
function main(){console.log({{ drop }});}const x = 100 > 42 ? x : y;
</script>

It should reindent with tabs when useTabs is true
useTabs: true
<script>
    function main(){
      console.log({{ drop }});
    }
    const x = 100 > 42 ? x : y;
</script>

It should respect embeddedSingleQuote
embeddedSingleQuote: false
<script>
console.log('hello');
</script>

It should not format Twig output as JS blocks
<script>
{{ output }}
</script>

It should not format Twig output as TypeScript blocks
<script type="application/x-typescript">
{{ output }}
</script>

It should not reindent template literals next to Twig
<div>
<script>
   foo(`a
     b {{ x | y }}`, {{ z }})
</script>
</div>

It should not reindent template literals when it can't parse the source
<div>
<script>
   foo(`a
     b`
</script>
</div>

It should reindent everything outside of a template literal
<div>
<script>
const a = `x`;
if (a) {
  c({{ z }});
}
</script>
<script>
const a = {{ z }};
if (a) {
  c(`x
    y`);
  d();
}
</script>
</div>

It should keep lines aligned when they could be inside a template literal
<div>
<script>
const a = `x`;
if (a) {
  c(`{{ z }}`);
}
</script>
</div>

It should format scripts that only contain Twig in strings
<script>
foo( '{{ x }}', "{{ path('a', {b: 'c'}) }}" )
foo( '{{ path('a') }}', '{{ a ~ '-' ~ b }}', 'a{{- x -}}b' )
a = { '{{ x }}': 1, 'b': y["{{ z }}"] }
</script>
<script type="application/x-typescript">
const a:string='{{ x }}'
</script>

It should keep the quotes of strings that contain Twig
embeddedSingleQuote: false
<script>
foo( 'a', '{{ json|raw }}' )
</script>

It should not format scripts that contain Twig outside of strings
<script>
foo( '{{ x }}', {{ y }} )
</script>
<script>
// {{ x }}
foo( '{{ y }}' )
</script>
<script>
foo( `{{ x }}` )
</script>
<script>
foo( /{{ x }}/ )
</script>
<script>
if (a) {{ b }}
</script>

It should not format scripts that contain Twig tags or comments
<script>
foo( '{% if a %}', 'b{% endif %}' )
</script>
<script>
foo( 'a{# c #}' )
</script>

It should not format scripts that contain Twig in strings whose contents would change
<script>
foo( 'it\'s {{ x }}' )
</script>
